t by the target position. For the first target I'm working out a starting release point with the updraft scaled to 4.28.\n\nI'm picking a starting release point for the heading-62 target: roughly 120 m of travel along that bearing, with the wind pushing the load back toward 205. I'll try a release at (-110, -58) and see where it lands."}, {"before_call": 28, "text": "I need to shift the release point by (+68, +68) to land at (-42, 10), but the smoke interaction could change that, so I'm holding off on entering smoke for now and will just try it."}, {"before_call": 29, "text": "I'm applying a shift of (+3.7, +9.2) and a release at (-38.3, 19.2). The smoke is making the response nonlinear, so I need to simulate again."}, {"before_call": 30, "text": "The target radius is 58.7 against 50 in the simulation, so I'm looking at whether I can test sensitivity to that gap. Scaling the geometry directly isn't an option, so I'm weighing whether to accept the mismatch or approximate a larger column. A longer path through the updraft column would raise the effective integrated lift by roughly the same 17%, which is the direction I'd need to check.\n\nThe real profile falls off more gently across the column than the simulated one, since 1-(r/58.7)\u00b2 stays higher than 1-(r/50)\u00b2 at mid radii. That suggests the effective updraft is perhaps 10-15% stronger in the region the load samples. I'll try the simulation with the updraft raised to about 4.7 and see how much the result moves."}, {"before_call": 31, "text": "Marking the sensitivity as insensitive at 1-2 m is fine. Drop target 1 works out to about (-943.3, 548.2). Averaging the two candidate positions leaves me adjusting the release point slightly, to about (-943.7, 547.5)."}, {"before_call": 32, "text": "I'm working through the second target's numbers: heading 115, altitude 93, speed 52, with a guessed release offset around (-45, 20) that I'm weighing against the earlier test's shift and the first target's (-38, 19) offset, and I'm leaning toward trying (-40, 25)."}, {"before_call": 33, "text": "I'm checking the entry point: the release has to shift by about (-2.2, +54.7) to reach the smoke, giving (-42.2, 79.7). The column radius is 36.7 in reality versus 50 in the sim, so I'll rerun with the shift and watch how much the radius mismatch matters. Afterward I want a no-updraft run to see how much the updraft actually affects the result."}, {"before_call": 35, "text": "The updraft only shifts things by about two meters, which is negligible. So I'll set the release point at roughly (-868.2, -1616.3), then nudge it slightly to account for the -1 adjustment, landing on about (-868.5, -1617)."}, {"before_call": 36, "text": "I'm working through Target 3 with an intensity of 0.6, an updraft of 1.86, heading 52, altitude 61, and speed 68. The unit direction is about (0.788, 0.616), so I'll guess a release point near (-70, -40) and run a simulation to check it."}, {"before_call": 37, "text": "Shift by (+16.9, +9.4): release (-43.1, -10.6)."}, {"before_call": 39, "text": "I'm working out the release values, taking the smaller R and the effect between the bounds, and the impact ranges look acceptable. That gives a release of about (1359.9, 1161.7)."}, {"before_call": 40, "text": "I'm checking target 4 now: its estimate is 0.87 with an updraft of 2.7, heading 51 and altitude 45, at a speed of 57. I'm going to guess the release point at (-50, -20)."}, {"before_call": 41, "text": "Shift (-0.1, -5.2): release (-40.1, -15.2). Check with updraft variants."}, {"before_call": 44, "text": "I'm working on target 5, with its values for the intensity, updraft, heading, altitude and speed. I'm estimating a release point near (-50, -20) and a direction vector, then comparing it to target 1's earlier offset, and I'll try an offset of (-45, 10) next."}, {"before_call": 45, "text": "Shift (+0.1, +22): release (-44.9, 32)."}, {"before_call": 46, "text": "I'm shifting the coordinates by (-1.3, -3.3), which puts 